Z||000009||beer_stud_21||05-23-2001||04:39 PM||||I think that pyrahna kit looks DOPE!  I never thought much of the 89 fieros.  And it seems like they needlessly lengthened the prototypes.  If AUS could make something close to what the pyrahna kit looks like I bet he would make a killing.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Nashco||05-23-2001||10:12 PM||||Needlessly lengthened...?  Beerstud, when was the last time you compared your trunk to a normal car's?  Not that we're going for a spacious car, but the fiero's space management was kind of poor.  I always wished the trunk was a touch bigger, so the spare could fit in it and still have room...then you'd have trunk space up front and out back.<P>Well, sorry for the interruption on the topic...I LOVE the Pyrahna kit...but I'm tired of the inability to get anything from/like it.  It's like trying to get a unicorn...<P>The second kit there isn't bad...I like it a lot except for the boxiness of the fender extensions.  I would prefer a gentle curve, but to each his own.  It does look very agressive.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000011||mrgone||05-23-2001||10:19 PM||||ohh...<P>*tear forming*||||reg||1
